                <pb facs="0746" n="650" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg650"/>

                <head>No. 446.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish to Mr. Morris.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Cable telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian" when="1870-06-04"
                                ><hi rendition="#small-caps">June</hi> 4, 1870</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi>, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Minister, Constantinople:</hi></p>
                <p>It is reported by telegraph that extensive murders of Jews have taken place in
                    Roumania. Ascertain facts, and, if true, unofficially urge on Turkish government
                    to put a stop to bloodshed. Answer by cable.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>FISH.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
